{"signature": "{\"text\": \"A non-renewable energy resource is used faster than it is naturally replaced on human timescales, so its accessible supply is finite. Coal, oil and natural gas are fossil fuels formed from ancient organic material over millions of years. They are extracted from the Earth and burnt to release energy from their chemical stores. Uranium is also a finite resource, but in a nuclear power station energy is released through nuclear fission rather than combustion.\", \"voice\": \"en-NG-AbeoNeural\", \"rate\": \"-4%\", \"eleven\": false}", "duration": 28.296, "words": [["A", 0.102083], ["non-renewable", 0.245333], ["energy", 0.896375], ["resource", 1.287], ["is", 1.716666], ["used", 1.912], ["faster", 2.159375], ["than", 2.523958], ["it", 2.680208], ["is", 2.823458], ["naturally", 2.953666], ["replaced", 3.422416], ["on", 3.878125], ["human", 4.034375], ["timescales,", 4.385958], ["so", 5.258333], ["its", 5.440625], ["accessible", 5.622916], ["supply", 6.195833], ["is", 6.5995], ["finite.", 6.716666], ["Coal,", 8.255208], ["oil", 8.763041], ["and", 9.114583], ["natural", 9.244791], ["gas", 9.700541], ["are", 9.960958], ["fossil", 10.091166], ["fuels", 10.45575], ["formed", 10.859375], ["from", 11.145833], ["ancient", 11.380208], ["organic", 11.770833], ["material", 12.213541], ["over", 12.734375], ["millions", 12.994791], ["of", 13.359375], ["years.", 13.502625], ["They", 14.895833], ["are", 15.117208], ["extracted", 15.286458], ["from", 15.898458], ["the", 16.145833], ["Earth", 16.289083], ["and", 16.5625], ["burnt", 16.783875], ["to", 17.005208], ["release", 17.135416], ["energy", 17.5], ["from", 17.916666], ["their", 18.151041], ["chemical", 18.346375], ["stores.", 18.763041], ["Uranium", 20.221375], ["is", 20.76825], ["also", 20.898458], ["a", 21.210958], ["finite", 21.276041], ["resource,", 21.757833], ["but", 22.591166], ["in", 22.786458], ["a", 22.890625], ["nuclear", 22.981791], ["power", 23.463541], ["station", 23.710958], ["energy", 24.1